course: dictionary
lesson: 9270
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have several meanings, and space is a good example. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» Here the clue is empty. Space means the area beyond the Earth's air, where the planets and stars are.
explain: «Teenage brothers need space.» Here space means room, the amount of area available to a person. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the word. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Space can be a noun or a verb.
fact: As a noun, space can mean the area beyond Earth's air, an empty area, room, a gap, or a period of time.
fact: As a verb, to space things means to put them with gaps between them.
fact: Common phrases with space include outer space, space station, personal space, take up space and make space.
fact: «When a crowd pushes, move to the side towards space» means move towards the open room, away from the squeeze.
exercise: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» What does space mean here? | A gap between two words | A period of time | *The area beyond Earth's air, where there is no air | A seat on a bus
exercise: «A coach is a big bus with luggage space underneath.» What does space mean here? | A gap between two words | To put things with gaps between them | *Room to put things in | The area beyond Earth's air
exercise: Which sentence uses space as a verb, meaning to put things with gaps between them? | I need some space to think | *Please space the chairs evenly across the hall | The space station orbits the Earth | There is no space left on the bus
test:  In the phrase «personal space», what does space mean? | The area beyond Earth's air | A gap between two words | A period of time | *The private area around a person
test:  In «in the space of an hour», what does space mean? | Room in a car | *A period of time | A gap between letters | The area beyond Earth's air
exam:  Jayden reads «There is no space left in the car.» What does space mean? | Outer space | *Room, the amount of area available | A period of time | A gap between two words
